estination</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.23 (0.55&#x02013;2.78)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.33 (0.53&#x02013;3.31)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02013;</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="TF7"><p><sup>a</sup>Odds ratio corrected by random effect and weight sampling.</p></fn><fn id="TF8"><p><sup>b</sup>Income minimum wage.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Association between area-level variables and hepatitis A infection, Northeast region, Midwest region and Federal district, Brazil, 2005</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead align="left"><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Northeast</th><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Central western</th><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Federal district</th></tr><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Area-level variables</th><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Odds ratio<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TF9"><sup>a</sup></xref> (95% CI)</th><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Odds ratio<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TF9"><sup>a</sup></xref> (95% CI)</th><th align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Odds ratio<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="TF9"><sup>a</sup></xref> (95% CI)</th></tr></thead><tbody align="left"><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Illiterate head of household (%)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.05 (1.03&#x02013;1.08)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.10 (1.05&#x02013;1.16)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.09 (1.03&#x02013;1.16)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Illiterate female head of household (%)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.13 (1.06&#x02013;1.21)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.27 (1.13&#x02013;1.44)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.04 (0.99&#x02013;1.09)</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Scho